s, Inc. in May 2004. Sonos, Inc. was incorporated in 2002 and is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas  Conrad | President, CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Sonos, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.0B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -4% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 44%.","The business throws off $123M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.61\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (23.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","c